def selection_sort(arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)-1):
        min_index = i
        for j in range(i+1, len(arr)):
            if arr[j] < arr[min_index]:
                min_index = j
        if min_index != i:
            arr[i], arr[min_index] = arr[min_index], arr[i]
    return arr
```

This function takes an array as input and returns the sorted array. It uses a loop to iterate through the array, finding the minimum element in each iteration and swapping it with the element at the current index. The minimum element is found at the end of the array, so the loop ends when it reaches the last element.

